        "kind": "question",
        "knowledgePoint": null,
        "markdown": "$\\frac{{6}^{6}}{{6}^{8}}=$",
        "mathAcademyId": "q-100368",
        "requiresCalculator": null,
        "solution": "To divide powers of the same base, we simply subtract the exponents:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{6}^{6}}{{6}^{8}}={6}^{6-8}={6}^{-2}\n$$\n\nTo evaluate ${6}^{-2},$ we find the reciprocal of the base $(6)$ and then raise that reciprocal to the same power but with the opposite sign:\n\n$$\n{6}^{-2}={\\left(\\frac{1}{6}\\right)}^{2}=\\frac{1}{6}\\times \\frac{1}{6}=\\frac{1}{36}\n$$",
        "status": "correct",
        "stepId": "17592186682458",
        "title": "Practice",
        "unanswered": false
