        "requiresCalculator": null,
        "solution": "- The matrix $P$ has $4$ rows and $4$ columns. So, its dimensions are $4\\times 4.$ $\\,\u2713$\n\n- The matrix $Q$ has $3$ rows and $4$ columns. So, its dimensions are $3\\times 4.$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- The matrix $R$ has $4$ rows and $4$ columns. So, its dimensions are $4\\times 4.$ $\\,\u2713$\n\nTherefore, only $P$ and $R$ are $4\\times 4$ matrices.",
