    "markdown": "Express $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{9t}}$ using power notation.",
    "mathAcademyId": "q-72817",
    "requiresCalculator": null,
    "solution": "First, we convert the radical to a fractional exponent:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{9t}}=\\frac{1}{(9t)^{1/3}}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we take the reciprocal and convert the exponent to a negative exponent:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{(9t)^{1/3}}=(9t)^{-1/3}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{9t}}=(9t)^{-1/3}\n$$",
